# Everything below is uploaded to the builder on EVERY deploy and used by
# nothing inside the image. It is not the main cost of a slow build — the three
# Chromium installs in Dockerfile.worker are — but it is the part that is pure
# waste, and it also invalidates the `COPY . .` layer whenever a stray file
# changes, forcing a rebuild of every step after it.

# Sample media and debug captures (~18MB, none of it shipped)
four-k-sample
logs
*.mp3
*.mp4
key-*.png
key-results.json

# Local build artefacts and tooling state
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
coverage
.claude
scripts/.spike-out

# Docs and infra configs the runtime never reads
*.md
fly*.toml
docker-compose.yml
supabase/migrations
